  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nHow many shrimp can Emily peel and saute in ten minutes? Emily can peel 7 shrimp per minute. Emily has 100 unpeeled shrimp available. Emily works continuously for the entire ten-minute period.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "LOSSY SELF-SUMMARY; VERIFY AGAINST NEW INPUTS\nVISIBLE PREFIX THROUGH TURN 1; LOSSY EXTRACT:\n- {\"content\":\"Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\\\boxed{}.\\n\\nHow many shrimp can Emily peel and saute in ten minutes? Emily can peel 7 shrimp per minute. Emily has 100 unpeeled shrimp available. Emily works con...\n- {\"content\":\"Emily can peel:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n7 \\\\text{ shrimp/minute} \\\\times 10 \\\\text{ minutes}=70\\\\text{ shrimp}.\\n\\\\]\\n\\nSince 100 shrimp are available, she has enough shrimp to maintain this rate. Therefore, she can peel and sauté\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\...",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Emily can peel 6 shrimp per minute.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel and sauté:\n\n\\[\n6\\text{ shrimp/minute}\\times 10\\text{ minutes}=60\\text{ shrimp}.\n\\]\n\nSince 60 is fewer than the 100 shrimp available, she can complete the work.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{60\\text{ shrimp}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Okay, now let me ask about just one part of that. How many shrimp can Emily peel in ten minutes? Additionally, Emily discards 5 shrimp after peeling them because they are damaged.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel:\n\n\\[\n6\\text{ shrimp/minute}\\times 10\\text{ minutes}=60\\text{ shrimp}.\n\\]\n\nShe then discards 5 damaged shrimp:\n\n\\[\n60-5=55\\text{ shrimp}.\n\\]\n\nThus, she can **peel \\(\\boxed{60}\\) shrimp** (of which \\(\\boxed{55}\\) remain after discarding the damaged ones).",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 12 minutes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily’s rates are:\n\n- Peeling: \\(6\\) shrimp/minute, so in 10 minutes she peels  \n  \\[\n  6\\times 10=60\\text{ shrimp}.\n  \\]\n- Sautéing:  \n  \\[\n  \\frac{30}{12}=2.5\\text{ shrimp/minute},\n  \\]\n  so in 10 minutes she can sauté  \n  \\[\n  2.5\\times 10=25\\text{ shrimp}.\n  \\]\n\nAlthough 60 shrimp are peeled and 5 are discarded, sautéing is the limiting step. Therefore, she can sauté\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{25\\text{ shrimp}}\n\\]\n\nin ten minutes.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 10 minutes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can:\n\n- Peel \\(6 \\times 10 = 60\\) shrimp.\n- Discard \\(5\\), leaving \\(60-5=55\\) usable shrimp.\n- Sauté \\(30\\) shrimp in 10 minutes.\n\nSince she has enough usable shrimp, sautéing is the limiting step. Thus, she can sauté\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{30\\text{ shrimp}}.\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Emily peels and sautes each shrimp sequentially rather than simultaneously.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Since Emily peels and sautés each shrimp sequentially:\n\n- Peeling time per shrimp:\n  \\[\n  \\frac{1}{6}\\text{ minute}\n  \\]\n- Sautéing time per shrimp:\n  \\[\n  \\frac{10}{30}=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{ minute}\n  \\]\n\nThus, each shrimp takes\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ minute}.\n\\]\n\nIn 10 minutes, she can process\n\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{1/2}=20\\text{ shrimp}.\n\\]\n\nAfter discarding 5 damaged shrimp, the number successfully sautéed is\n\n\\[\n20-5=\\boxed{15\\text{ shrimp}}.\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Got it. But now I only need to know about: How long will it take Emily to peel and cook the shrimp? By the way, Emily needs to peel and cook 90 shrimp.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily’s rates are:\n\n- Peeling: \\(6\\) shrimp per minute, so each shrimp takes  \n  \\[\n  \\frac{1}{6}\\text{ minute}.\n  \\]\n- Sautéing: \\(30\\) shrimp in \\(10\\) minutes, so each shrimp takes  \n  \\[\n  \\frac{10}{30}=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{ minute}.\n  \\]\n\nBecause she works sequentially, the time per shrimp is\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ minute}.\n\\]\n\nSince 5 shrimp are discarded, she must process \\(90+5=95\\) shrimp to end up with 90 cooked shrimp:\n\n\\[\n95\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=47.5\\text{ minutes}.\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{47.5\\text{ minutes}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
